---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DemoShell from '../../components/DemoShell.astro';
import Control from '../../components/demos/Control.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/url';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="EIS / DRT analyser"
  description="Paste or drop an impedance spectrum and get its Nyquist and Bode plots, its distribution of relaxation times, and a table of peaks with resistances and time constants. Computed entirely in your browser."
  section="/tools/"
  ogImage="posters/og-tools-eis.png"
>
  <div class="page" id="eis-page">
    <article class="prose">
      <span class="overline">Tool</span>
      <h1>EIS / DRT analyser</h1>
      <p>
        Paste an impedance spectrum, or drop a file on the box, and this page inverts it to a
        distribution of relaxation times: which processes are in the cell, at what timescale, and
        how much resistance each one carries. It is the same Tikhonov-regularised non-negative
        least-squares inversion as the <a href={withBase('/demos/#demo-impedance')}>impedance demo</a>,
        pointed at your data instead of a built-in circuit.
      </p>
      <p class="tool-privacy">
        Everything is computed in this tab. Your data is not uploaded: there is no server behind
        this site to upload it to.
      </p>
    </article>

    <section class="panel eis-input" aria-labelledby="eis-input-h">
      <h2 class="overline" id="eis-input-h">1 · Data</h2>
      <label class="visually-hidden" for="eis-input">Impedance data: frequency, real part, imaginary part</label>
      <textarea
        id="eis-input"
        spellcheck="false"
        rows="7"
        placeholder="f / Hz, Z′ / Ω, Z″ / Ω — one row per frequency. Comma, tab, semicolon or space separated; a header row is optional."
      ></textarea>
      <div class="eis-input-row">
        <label class="tool-btn eis-file">
          choose a file
          <input type="file" id="eis-file" accept=".csv,.tsv,.txt,.dat,.z,text/*" />
        </label>
        <button class="tool-btn" type="button" id="eis-example">load the example</button>
        <button class="tool-btn" type="button" id="eis-clear">clear</button>
        <span class="eis-source" id="eis-source"></span>
      </div>
      <p class="eis-status" id="eis-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading…</p>
      <details class="eis-columns">
        <summary>Columns were read wrong?</summary>
        <div class="eis-columns-grid">
          <label>frequency <select id="eis-col-f"></select></label>
          <label>real part Z′ <select id="eis-col-re"></select></label>
          <label>imaginary part <select id="eis-col-im"></select></label>
          <label class="eis-check"><input type="checkbox" id="eis-negated" /> that column holds −Z″</label>
        </div>
      </details>
    </section>

    <DemoShell
      id="tool-eis"
      code="2"
      title="Spectrum and DRT"
      poster="d4-impedance.svg"
      alt="Nyquist plot, Bode magnitude and phase, and the distribution of relaxation times for an impedance spectrum"
      aspect="16/10"
      stack={true}
      caption="Points are your data; the dashed curve is the spectrum rebuilt from the DRT. In the DRT panel, the dotted lines bound the measured window and each numbered line is a peak in the table below."
    >
      <fieldset class="panel" slot="panel" disabled>
        <legend>inversion</legend>
        <div class="control-cols">
          <Control id="eis-lambda" label="λ (Tikhonov)" min={1e-5} max={10} value={1e-2} scale="log" />
          <Control id="eis-ntau" label="τ bins" min={30} max={120} value={60} step={10} />
        </div>
        <div class="switch-row">
          <label><input type="checkbox" id="eis-drop-inductive" checked /> exclude inductive points (Im Z &gt; 0)</label>
        </div>
      </fieldset>
    </DemoShell>

    <section class="eis-results" aria-labelledby="eis-peaks-h">
      <div class="eis-results-head">
        <h2 id="eis-peaks-h">Peaks</h2>
        <button class="tool-btn" type="button" id="eis-export-peaks">export table as csv</button>
      </div>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>#</th>
              <th class="num">τ</th>
              <th class="num">f = 1/(2πτ)</th>
              <th class="num">R (area)</th>
              <th class="num">C = τ/R</th>
              <th>share of Σ R</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody id="eis-peaks"><tr><td colspan="6">Computing…</td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="eis-summary" id="eis-summary"></p>
    </section>

    <section class="eis-sweep" aria-labelledby="eis-sweep-h">
      <div class="eis-results-head">
        <h2 id="eis-sweep-h">Choosing λ</h2>
        <button class="tool-btn" type="button" id="eis-sweep-png">png</button>
      </div>
      <p class="prose">
        There is no neutral choice of λ. Too small and noise turns into sharp spikes that look
        like processes; too large and separate processes merge into one hump. What can be checked
        is stability: a peak that is really in the data survives a decade or more of λ. The plots
        below repeat the inversion over four decades. Look for the range where the peak count sits
        still while the misfit has not yet started to climb.
      </p>
      <div class="demo-stage eis-sweep-stage split-stage-host">
        <div class="split-stage" id="eis-sweep-stage"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="eis-suggest">
        <button class="tool-btn" type="button" id="eis-suggest" disabled>use the centre of the stable range</button>
        <span id="eis-suggest-out" role="status"></span>
      </div>
      <p class="eis-caveat">
        The suggestion is a heuristic for where to start, not a claim that the value is correct.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose eis-limits" aria-labelledby="eis-limits-h">
      <h2 id="eis-limits-h">What this does and does not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Read areas, not heights.</strong> γ is a density in ln τ. The area under a peak is
          the resistance of that process and does not depend on the τ grid; the height does, and a
          sharp process gets taller as you add bins.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Capacitive processes only.</strong> The model is R<sub>∞</sub> plus a non-negative
          sum of RC relaxations, every one of which has Im Z ≤ 0. Inductive points cannot be
          represented, so they are excluded by default and shown in a different colour.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Diffusion is a band, not a peak.</strong> A Warburg element has no single
          relaxation time. It appears as a broad band, often running off the slow end of the window.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Peaks outside the measured window are extrapolation.</strong> The τ grid extends a
          decade past your data at each end. Peaks there are flagged in the table.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No data-quality test.</strong> This page does not run a Kramers–Kronig check. If the
          cell drifted during the measurement, the DRT will faithfully invert the drift.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Units pass through.</strong> Frequencies are read as Hz and impedances as Ω. If
          yours are Ω·cm², the resistances are Ω·cm² and the capacitances F/cm².
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The method is written up on the <a href={withBase('/physics/impedance/')}>impedance page</a>,
        and its recovery of a known circuit is checked live on the
        <a href={withBase('/validation/')}>validation page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .tool-privacy {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    padding-left: var(--s3);
  }

  .eis-input {
    margin-top: var(--s6);
  }

  .eis-input > .overline {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--s3);
  }

  textarea {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    resize: vertical;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--fg);
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--s3);
  }

  textarea[data-drop] {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    border-style: dashed;
  }

  .eis-input-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--s2);
    margin-top: var(--s3);
  }

  /* The native file input is kept (it is what makes the label keyboard
     reachable) and visually collapsed into the button-styled label. */
  .eis-file {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .eis-file input {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    opacity: 0;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .eis-file:focus-within {
    outline: 3px solid var(--focus);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .eis-source {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }

  .eis-status {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--badge-shipped-fg);
    margin-top: var(--s3);
  }

  .eis-status[data-bad] {
    color: var(--check-fail-fg);
  }

  .eis-columns {
    margin-top: var(--s3);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .eis-columns summary {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    cursor: pointer;
    width: fit-content;
  }

  .eis-columns-grid {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--s3) var(--s5);
    margin-top: var(--s3);
  }

  .eis-columns-grid label {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--s2);
  }

  .eis-results,
  .eis-sweep,
  .eis-limits {
    margin-top: var(--s7);
  }

  .eis-results-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--s3);
    margin-bottom: var(--s3);
  }

  /* The site's table headers are small caps, which turns τ into Τ and π into Π. */
  .eis-results th {
    text-transform: none;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .eis-results :global(tr.is-extrapolated td) {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }

  .eis-summary,
  .eis-caveat {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }

  .eis-sweep .prose {
    margin-bottom: var(--s4);
  }

  .eis-sweep-stage {
    aspect-ratio: 3/1;
  }

  .eis-suggest {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--s3);
    margin: var(--s3) 0 var(--s2);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .eis-sweep-stage {
      aspect-ratio: 3/4;
    }

    :global(#tool-eis .demo-stage) {
      aspect-ratio: 9/16 !important;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  import { getShell } from '../../components/demos/runtime';
  import { init } from '../../components/tools/eis-analyser';

  const shell = getShell('tool-eis');
  const page = document.getElementById('eis-page');
  if (shell && page) {
    try {
      init(shell, page);
    } catch (err) {
      const status = document.getElementById('eis-status');
      if (status) {
        status.textContent = 'The analyser failed to start. Reload the page to retry.';
        status.setAttribute('data-bad', '');
      }
      console.error('[voltaire:tool-eis]', err);
    }
  }
</script>
